        drivingExperience: "The G82 M4 CSL (Coupe Sport Leichtbau) is the most hardcore, uncompromising road-legal M4 ever created, limited to just 1,000 units globally. BMW stripped 100kg of weight by removing the rear seats, installing fixed carbon bucket seats, carbon fiber trunk lid, and a bespoke titanium exhaust. It is exclusively Rear-Wheel Drive. The S58 engine is pushed to 550 horsepower. Due to reduced sound deadening, every gear whine, turbo spool, and the terrifyingly loud titanium exhaust crackle is transmitted directly into the cabin. The suspension is rigidly track-focused with bespoke cast-aluminum strut braces. It is a violent, raw, and incredibly demanding driving machine that requires total respect.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The S58 engine in the M4 CSL is an absolute masterpiece. The 550hp output is achieved through higher factory boost (2.1 bar) and optimized software, meaning the engine is identical mechanically to the base M4 and still vastly under-stressed. The closed-deck block is virtually indestructible. However, you must remain vigilant about the modern BMW plastic cooling components, specifically the Heat Management Module and the top-mount intercooler, which will inevitably leak. If you unlock the DME, delete the OPF, and swap the plastic charge pipes, you have a bulletproof, outrageously fast hypercar killer. Be aware that replacing any of the bespoke CSL parts (like the carbon fiber trunk or the specific red-accented grilles) will cost a small fortune.",
        repairCostEstimate: "$2,500 - $5,000+ / year (The S58 is mechanically bulletproof, but the CSL is a hyper-rare special edition M-car. The running costs are extremely high. Routine maintenance includes 7.0L of expensive synthetic oil, M-specific diff fluid, and massive, expensive Carbon Ceramic brake rotors. Budget for occasional plastic cooling system repairs (Heat Management Module: 300 EUR). The bespoke carbon fiber exterior parts, titanium exhaust, and specialized cast-aluminum strut braces are astronomically expensive to replace if damaged. Prepare your wallet, but the reliability is exceptional)."
